  "source": "USC Optical Sound Effects Library (archive.org/details/usc-sound-effect-archive)",
  "source_note": "Red Library: first-generation copies of 1930s-40s nitrate optical sound effects collected by a Hollywood sound editor, donated to USC, transferred to tape by USC Cinema students in the early 1970s, digitised by Craig Smith (Academic Sound Coordinator, CalArts School of Film/Video) and uploaded to the Internet Archive by jscott@archive.org under CC0 1.0. Bandwidth is optical-era (99% of energy under ~5-8 kHz) and the transfers are unrestored — which is why these are a base layer under the generators' own high band, not a drop-in replacement.",
  "verified": "2026-08-09 — licenseurl CC0 1.0 on every item, uploader jscott@archive.org (Internet Archive staff), collection usc-sound-effect-archive carries a written donation history",
  "note": "Vendored so the gen_*.py generators rebuild without a network. These are trimmed single contacts, denoised and levelled; the untrimmed originals are at the source_url of each entry. Each generator falls back to fully-procedural if this directory is missing, so a clean checkout still builds.",
  "rebuild": "tools/audio/.venv/bin/python tools/audio/fetch_sources.py",
